description:
Depends on: none.

Own the GE command stream before any pixel work. Add `runtime/ge/display_list.*`:
- decode 32-bit GE command words (opcode + 24-bit argument), NOP/END/RET/FINISH/SIGNAL, JUMP/CALL/RET with the 24-bit address rules, base/offset and stall/update-stall;
- decode primitive/VTYPE packets and vertex layouts into typed commands, not raw words;
- bounded execution: jump/call stack depth, loop/cycle cap, unknown opcode -> named error (never a silent skip);
- emit a deterministic decoded trace consumed by the CPU front end and the Vulkan backend.

Tests (red-first, hand-authored synthetic words only): opcode/argument extraction; jump/call/ret; stall; END/FINISH; unknown opcode trap; loop bound; deterministic trace. Acceptance: a `tests/ge` fixture builds and passes; the decoder has no Vulkan dependency.

Specific searches: `gh search code "GeCommand" --extension cpp`; `gh search code "sceGeListEnQueue" --extension cpp`; `gh search code "GeDisplayList" --extension cpp`. Refs: Zig-PSP `src/ge/commands.zig`, PPSSPP `Core/HLE/sceGe.cpp`, KanaStation `src/core/hw/ge/ge.cpp`.

Reference discovery (all tasks): before implementing, use `gh search code "<api-or-symbol>"` (add `--extension cpp` for C/C++ HLE work) to find concrete implementations and their projects, then `gh search issues "<api-or-symbol>"` for semantics and regressions. Record the references used.

Reference snapshot (2026-10-30): AdamFull/psprecore (MIT, 605bd096) `runtime/src/ge.cpp` and `runtime/include/psprecore/runtime/ge.hpp` implement this walker closely: command map, BASE/OFFSET, VADDR/IADDR, CALL/RET with saved offset, SIGNAL/FINISH/END, a 10M guard and `VertexFormat::decode`. Use as a behavioral oracle or port source with attribution; it depends on `nx-foundation`, which has no LICENSE, so port to std rather than vendoring that subtree.
